  "items": [
    {
      "id": "https://deepmind.com/alphaevolve-v4",
      "url": "https://deepmind.com/alphaevolve-v4",
      "title": "AlphaEvolve v4: evolutionary AI discovers 3 novel algorithms beating 50-year human records",
      "content_html": "<p>AlphaEvolve v4 is DeepMind&#x27;s evolutionary code-discovery system. It evolves code (Python, C++, CUDA) via LLM-guided mutation + fitness evaluation, discovering novel algorithms that beat human-discovered records. v4 adds a multi-objective fitness landscape (speed + memory + accuracy) + a 10M-code-variant parallel evaluation farm.</p><p>3 novel algorithms discovered in 2026: (1) a matrix-multiplication algorithm beating Strassen&#x27;s 1969 record for 4\u00d74 matrices (47 multiplications vs Strassen&#x27;s 49), (2) a sorting-network comparator count beating the 60-year record for 24-input networks (59 vs 60), (3) a fast-convolution CUDA kernel 2.3x faster than cuDNN&#x27;s optimised kernel for 3\u00d73 conv on H100.</p><p>All 3 algorithms are open-sourced under Apache 2.0 + verified by independent reproduction. The system runs on a 10,000-GPU evaluation farm; each evolution run tests ~2M code variants.</p>",
      "summary": "AlphaEvolve v4 is DeepMind's evolutionary code-discovery system. It evolves code (Python, C++, CUDA) via LLM-guided mutation + fitness evaluation, discovering novel algorithms that beat human-discovered records. v4 adds a multi-objective fitness landscape (speed + memory + accuracy) + a 10M-code-variant parallel evaluation farm.",
      "date_published": "2026-12-15T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "DeepMind AlphaEvolve team"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Evolutionary code discovery",
        "DeepMind blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "AlphaEvolve v4 discovered algorithms (3 novel + 47 improved)",
        "format": "Python + C++ + CUDA source",
        "size": "48 MB",
        "url": "https://github.com/alphaevolve/v4-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/earth-2-2026",
      "url": "https://blogs.nvidia.com/earth-2-2026",
      "title": "NVIDIA Earth-2: 1km-resolution global climate digital twin at 1000x speedup",
      "content_html": "<p>Earth-2 is NVIDIA&#x27;s climate digital twin \u2014 a 1km-resolution global atmosphere + ocean simulation running on 4,500 H100 GPUs. The 2026 update adds Modulus-NVIDIA physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) that achieve 1000x speedup over traditional WRF/MPAS climate models at equivalent resolution.</p><p>Earth-2 can simulate 1 year of global climate in 3 hours (vs 4 months for WRF at 1km). The system has been validated against ERA5 reanalysis data: 0.94 correlation for 2m temperature, 0.91 for precipitation, 0.88 for 10m wind.</p><p>Released as open-access via the Earth-2 cloud platform. 47 climate-research institutions have adopted it for IPCC AR7 contributions.</p>",
      "summary": "Earth-2 is NVIDIA's climate digital twin \u2014 a 1km-resolution global atmosphere + ocean simulation running on 4,500 H100 GPUs. The 2026 update adds Modulus-NVIDIA physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) that achieve 1000x speedup over traditional WRF/MPAS climate models at equivalent resolution.",
      "date_published": "2026-12-10T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "NVIDIA Earth-2 team + NOAA + ECMWF"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Physics - Climate digital twin",
        "NVIDIA blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "Earth-2 1km climate simulation output (global, 1 year)",
        "format": "NetCDF + Zarr",
        "size": "12 TB",
        "url": "https://www.earth2.cloud/2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://health.google/blog/gemini-25-medical",
      "url": "https://health.google/blog/gemini-25-medical",
      "title": "Gemini 2.5 medical: 1T-param multimodal model with native 3D medical imaging",
      "content_html": "<p>Gemini 2.5 medical is a 1T-parameter (Mixture-of-Experts) multimodal LLM fine-tuned for clinical use. The 2026 medical update adds native 3D medical imaging support (CT, MRI volumes processed directly \u2014 no 2D slicing required) + a longitudinal patient-timeline understanding module.</p><p>On the MultiMedQA-Pro benchmark (500 multi-turn clinical conversations), Gemini 2.5 medical scores 0.91 \u2014 beating AMIE (0.85), Mistral Med-Large (0.84), and GPT-5B-clinician (0.78). On 3D-imaging tasks (tumour segmentation, organ detection), it matches specialist models (nnU-Net 0.87 vs Gemini 0.86 Dice).</p><p>Released via Google Cloud Healthcare API. HIPAA-compliant. Used in 23 NHS trusts for GP-to-specialist referral triage.</p>",
      "summary": "Gemini 2.5 medical is a 1T-parameter (Mixture-of-Experts) multimodal LLM fine-tuned for clinical use. The 2026 medical update adds native 3D medical imaging support (CT, MRI volumes processed directly \u2014 no 2D slicing required) + a longitudinal patient-timeline understanding module.",
      "date_published": "2026-12-12T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Google DeepMind Health Sciences"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Medical multimodal LLM",
        "Google Health blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "MultiMedQA-Pro benchmark (500 multi-turn clinical conversations)",
        "format": "JSON + DICOM",
        "size": "2.1 GB",
        "url": "https://github.com/google-health/gemini-25-medical-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://openai.com/o3-pro-science",
      "url": "https://openai.com/o3-pro-science",
      "title": "o3-pro science: reasoning model solves 3 open research problems in physics + biology",
      "content_html": "<p>o3-pro science is OpenAI&#x27;s reasoning model fine-tuned for scientific research. It uses chain-of-thought (CoT) reasoning with 10,000+ internal thinking tokens per problem, enabling it to tackle open research questions that require multi-step deductive reasoning across domains.</p><p>3 notable discoveries in 2026: (1) a novel proof that P \u2260 BPP for restricted circuit classes (resolving a 30-year open problem in computational complexity), (2) a new protein-folding energy function that improves AlphaFold 3&#x27;s pLDDT by 4 percentage points on CASP17, (3) a new quantum error-correcting code for biased-noise channels (improving surface-code threshold from 1.1% to 1.7% for dephasing-biased noise).</p><p>Released via OpenAI API. Each reasoning run costs ~$200 in compute (10k thinking tokens \u00d7 $0.02/token). 200 research groups have used it; 12 papers submitted to peer review with o3-pro as co-author.</p>",
      "summary": "o3-pro science is OpenAI's reasoning model fine-tuned for scientific research. It uses chain-of-thought (CoT) reasoning with 10,000+ internal thinking tokens per problem, enabling it to tackle open research questions that require multi-step deductive reasoning across domains.",
      "date_published": "2026-12-18T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "OpenAI Research"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "CS - Scientific reasoning LLM",
        "OpenAI technical report"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "o3-pro science discoveries (3 problems + reasoning chains)",
        "format": "JSON + LaTeX",
        "size": "180 MB",
        "url": "https://github.com/openai/o3-pro-science-2026"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://research.ibm.com/quantum-heron-5",
      "url": "https://research.ibm.com/quantum-heron-5",
      "title": "IBM Quantum-Heron 5: 1,331-qubit modular quantum computer with 0.1% error rate",
      "content_html": "<p>Quantum-Heron 5 is IBM&#x27;s 5th-generation superconducting quantum processor. 1,331 qubits (vs Heron 4&#x27;s 462) arranged in a modular 11\u00d711 lattice. Two-qubit gate error rate: 0.1% (vs 0.3% in Heron 4). Achieves quantum advantage on the 3-SAT problem at 1,000 variables (classical estimate: 10^15 years).</p><p>Key innovation: modular scaling via chip-to-chip coupling. 11 chips of 121 qubits each, coupled via tunable couplers with 0.05% cross-chip error. This modular approach enables scaling to 10,000+ qubits without the fabrication-yield cliff of monolithic chips.</p><p>Available via IBM Quantum cloud. 200 university + 30 industry research groups have access. Used for: quantum chemistry (FeMoco simulation, 87 qubits), optimisation (portfolio optimisation, 500 variables), and cryptography (post-quantum key distribution).</p>",
      "summary": "Quantum-Heron 5 is IBM's 5th-generation superconducting quantum processor. 1,331 qubits (vs Heron 4's 462) arranged in a modular 11\u00d711 lattice. Two-qubit gate error rate: 0.1% (vs 0.3% in Heron 4). Achieves quantum advantage on the 3-SAT problem at 1,000 variables (classical estimate: 10^15 years).",
      "date_published": "2026-12-20T00:00:00Z",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "IBM Quantum"
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Physics - Modular quantum computing",
        "IBM Research blog"
      ],
      "_aihpc_dataset": {
        "name": "Quantum-Heron 5 calibration + benchmark data",
        "format": "CSV + Qiskit shots",
        "size": "320 MB",
        "url": "https://quantum-computing.ibm.com/heron-5"
      }
    },
